BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:This traveling exhibit tells the stories of seven everyday Nort
 h Carolinians and extraordinary leaders — Gertrude Weil\, Henry Owl\, Joe L
 ewis\, Abraham Galloway\, Ronald Mace\, James Hunter\, and Willa Player — w
 ho petitioned\, protested\, and organized to expand democracy. The exhibit 
 explores change\, freedom\, civic responsibility\, and overcoming challenge
 s by telling the story of a few North Carolinians who have raised their voi
 ces to call out injustice and fully participate in our democratic society.
DTEND:20260408T040000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035719Z
DTSTART:20260407T130000Z
GEO:35.596641;-82.55485
LOCATION:Pack Memorial Library \, Main level
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:"Making Our Voices Heard: North Carolinians Fighting for Civil Righ
 ts" Exhibit
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52136240434760
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/making-our-voices-heard-north-carolini
 ans-fighting-for-civil-rights-exhibit
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:In commemoration of America's 250th\, Atkins Library at UNC Cha
 rlotte presents the exhibit "Charlotte\, A Hornet’s Nest of Rebellion: An E
 nduring Legacy from the Revolutionary War to Today." Using archives and rar
 e books\, the exhibit tells the story of how Charlotte earned this reputati
 on\, tracing the history from British General Charles Cornwallis’s 1780 ret
 reat from our region to sports mascots and modern-day social activism. Plea
 se check the Atkins Library website for open hours.
DTEND:20260407T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035719Z
DTSTART:20260407T130000Z
GEO:35.305264;-80.730475
LOCATION:J. Murrey Atkins Library\, UNC Charlotte\, Atrium
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Charlotte: A Hornet's Nest of Rebellion
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52313356764478
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/charlotte-a-hornets-nest-of-rebellion
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Exhibitions,Celebrations & Commemorations,Cerem
 onies & Anniversaries,Open Houses
DESCRIPTION:You are invited to explore the history of Davie County as the S
 emiquincentennial draws closer. There will be historical artifacts on displ
 ay representing the county's history. This includes a portrait of Continent
 al Army Colonel William R. Davie\, the county's namesake. There's also a lo
 t of information on Daniel Boone\, who lived in Davie County for seven year
 s. His parents are buried in Mocksville's Joppa Cemetery. Feel free to brow
 se around the room and examine historical records and documents\, including
  a list of those who served during the American Revolution. \n\nThese artif
 acts and documents are located inside the Martin-Wall History Room within t
 he Davie County Public Library in Mocksville. This room acts as the Davie C
 ounty history museum. Paying a visit will allow you to explore the county's
  long and proud history while gaining a better understanding of the Semiqui
 ncentennial's significance. These artifacts will be on display from Monday\
 , March 16\, until at least Sunday\, July 6.
DTEND:20260407T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035719Z
DTSTART:20260407T130000Z
GEO:35.897815;-80.5597
LOCATION:Davie County Public Library\, Martin-Wall History Room
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:History on Display
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52372920365879
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/history-on-display
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Workshops & Trainings
DESCRIPTION:Join other K-5 classroom and nonformal educators as we explore 
 Project Learning Tree activities focused on birds.\n\nTogether for Birds is
  PLT’s Newest Activity Collection!\n\nBirds are a wonderful introduction to
  the natural world and happen to be just outside your door! Whether in the 
 city or a forest\, a variety of birds are usually within easy eyeshot or ea
 rshot. The activities are designed for educators to use with students in gr
 ades K-2\, with variations for grades 3-5. The collection is filled with en
 hanced bird-specific content such as new enrichment experiences\, recommend
 ed reading\, forest facts\, accompanying posters\, and charts. Every partic
 ipant will leave with a guide of this collection.\n\nThis workshop counts t
 oward NC Environmental Education Certification (Criteria I) and consists of
  six contact hours that may count toward CEUs for teachers.\n\n \n\nLocatio
 n: Carolina Beach State Park \nWorkshop Cost: $25\nThe PLT activity guides 
 are provided free of charge to participants through support from the NC For
 estry.\nFor additional workshop information\, call 910-772-0546.
DTEND:20260407T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035719Z
DTSTART:20260407T130000Z
GEO:34.045859;-77.905159
LOCATION:Carolina Beach State Park
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Project Learning Tree - Together for Birds
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51904311135329
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/project-learning-tree-together-for-bir
 ds
END:VEVENT
