BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions,Exhibits & Tours
DESCRIPTION:April 14th is the opening day for a new year-long exhibit at Ch
 arlotte Museum of History!\n\nAmerican Revolution\, the Augmented Exhibitio
 n immerses you in the key moments of the American Revolution that shaped Am
 erican democracy.\n\nThanks to the HistoPad\, visitors travel back in time 
 between 1767 and 1789 to discover immersive 3D reconstructions of 15 signif
 icant events of the revolution. Along the way\, they will explore events su
 ch as the Boston Tea Party\, the Constitutional Convention\, and the Battle
  of Yorktown\, as well as iconic cities and places such as Boston\, Philade
 lphia\, New York\, Canada\, and France.\n\nDeveloped in partnership with re
 nowned historians and researchers\, American Revolution\, the Augmented Exh
 ibition celebrates the diverse characters who have shaped American democrac
 y and combines the best of physical scenography and augmented reality to pr
 ovide an immersive historical experience for all ages. This exhibit is an o
 pportunity to present the revolution in a new way\, one that speaks to the 
 hearts and minds of today's American people.\n\nExhibit open through April 
 2027. \n\n www.charlottemuseum.org
DTSTAMP:20260508T035719Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260414
GEO:35.23394;-80.766646
LOCATION:Charlotte Museum of History
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Opening Day: American Revolution: the Augmented Experience
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51250118370852
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/american-revolution-the-augmented-expe
 rience
END:VEVENT
