DESCRIPTION:Eagles Island is more than a backdrop for the city of Wilmingto
 n—it is a place shaped by centuries of human experience and natural change.
  From its prehistoric uses to serving as the present-day home of the Battle
 ship North Carolina\, Eagles Island holds stories that are still unfolding.
  This talk invites you to see the island from the unique perspective of his
 torian and archaeologist Dr. Jay C. Martin\, Executive Director of the Batt
 leship North Carolina Memorial.\n\nTuesday\, April 21\, 2026 | 6:00 - 7:30 
 PM\nBattleship North Carolina Wardroom\n1 Battleship Road\, Wilmington\, NC
 \n\nAdmission:\n$5 advance online registration\n$8 at the door\nFriends Mem
 bers: Free\n\nSpace is limited! To reserve your spot\, visit bit.ly/eagles-
 island-history
