CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation,Nature & Wildlife Programs
DESCRIPTION:Spend Earth Day 2026 with us here at the North Carolina Zoo!\n\
 n\nBring us your old cell phones\, tablets or other hand-held electronics t
 o the Zoo to recycle at the Gorilla habitat! Zoo Staff and Keepers will be 
 at the Gorilla Habitat overlook from 10 a.m. - 2 p.m. where you can recycle
  your old electronic device and learn about how recycling old electronics c
 an directly impact gorillas in the wild! We can help you declutter and you 
 help preserve wild gorilla habitat! \n\n\nStop by Kidzone from 10 a.m. - 2 
 p.m. in North America to participate in the City Nature Challenge BioBlitz.
  Participants will earn native pollinator seeds and possibly even a pollina
 tor plant to take home. We will have tablets with iNaturalist on them so gu
 ests can see how it works and can practice on native wildlife in Kidzone. W
 e’ll have lots of NC native Animal Ambassadors throughout the day and table
 s where guests can learn more about the different types of animals (and pla
 nts) that they may find. \n\n\nBoth of these events are free with Zoo admis
 sion. Happy Earth Day!
DTEND:20260422T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035720Z
DTSTART:20260422T140000Z
GEO:35.629422;-79.764409
LOCATION:North Carolina Zoo
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Earth Day at the Zoo 
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52649479844284
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/earth-day-at-the-zoo
