BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
DESCRIPTION:Join us as the community of Norwood and Stanly County commemora
 tes the Revolutionary Battle of Colson's Mill that occurred July 21\, 1780.
   A mural depicting this battle was designed and painted by local mural art
 ists\, Jack and Eli Williams of Williams Brothers Murals\, Albemarle\, NC. 
 \n\nColson’s Mill was one of the first Patriot victories in the Southern Ca
 mpaign of the American Revolution. It encouraged other Colonists to support
  the American War of Independence.\n\nAfter the victory at Colson’s\, the w
 inds of war shifted with subsequent victories at Kings Mountain and Cowpens
 . The wider campaign continued through Guilford Courthouse\, and ultimately
 \, Yorktown\, where the British surrendered.\n\nWho are the artists of the 
 Colson Mill mural?\n\nWMS Brothers\, Jack and Eli Williams were born and ra
 ised in Albemarle\, NC\, and grew up with an art-teacher as a father. Their
  love of painting was sparked at a young age. They began creating large-sca
 le work in 2015\, but officially started painting murals in 2020. Each brot
 her brings their our own strengths but combine them into one collaborative 
 voice.\n\nArtist Vision for the Battle of Colson’s Mill mural:\n\n“This pie
 ce is an abstract interpretation of the Battle at Colson’s Mill. Our inspir
 ation came from the cubist art style. We used sharp angles\, broken shapes\
 , and bold color block to capture the chaos\, speed\, and intensity of the 
 battle.\nOn the left\, the blue forms with white marks represent the Patrio
 t militia. On the right\, the reds and oranges symbolize the Loyalists. The
  mill sits at center of the mural. The flowing shapes along the bottom of t
 he mural represent the meeting point of the Pee Dee River and Rocky River.\
 nThe entire composition is meant to feel loud and full of motion.”\n\nThis 
 mural was funded by a grant from America 250 NC.
DTEND:20260425T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035720Z
DTSTART:20260425T150000Z
GEO:35.225422;-80.120008
LOCATION:Outdoor Art Gallery
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Battle of Colson's Mill - Mural Unveiling
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52640478143107
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/battle-of-colsons-mill-mural-unveiling
END:VEVENT
