BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations,Reenactments & Living History,Exhi
 bits & Tours,Special Site Programs
DESCRIPTION:Join us to commemorate the surrender negotiations at Bennett Pl
 ace that led to the largest surrender of the American Civil War. Learn more
  about how Generals Johnston and Sherman's three meetings at the Bennetts' 
 home reflected the broader national debate over how to reunite the nation &
  remake the United States without slavery. Explore how veterans\, civilians
 \, and freed people alike experienced and thought about the end of the Amer
 ican Civil War and what would come next.\n\nThis program includes several c
 ostumed interpretation events and displays.\n\nTickets must be purchased on
  site the day of the event.\n\nSchedule of Events:\n\nTalks & Presentations
 \n\n11:00  The Road to Bennett Place - Ranger Talk\n\n12:00  "Civil War Rai
 lroads in NC: Development & Impact on the War" - Presentation by Dr. Ted Ku
 nstling\, MD (Raleigh Civil War Round Table President)\n\n1:00*  The Story 
 from the Land - Environmental History Walking Tour (*time may change)\n\n2:
 00  Surrender & Freedom Stories - Presentation\n\n2:30  What Comes Next?: A
 ftermath of the Civil War - Ranger Talk\n\nSurrender Vignettes 11:30\, 11:5
 0\, 12:10\, 1:20\, and 1:40\n\nLimited spaces available inside the Bennett 
 home! Be in the room where it happened while our site historians walk throu
 gh the surrender negotiations. Features Sherman and Johnston reenactors. (1
 5 minutes) Advance registration link via Eventbrite - some tickets availabl
 e same-day. Advanced registration recommended.\n\nFree Flowing Stations Exp
 lore at your own pace from 11:00 - 3:00. Most stations include hands-on edu
 cation.\n\nCivil War EngineeringSignal FlagsMorse CodeCivilians on the Home
 frontUS & Confederate soldiers at the end of the warPlease note due to the 
 current drought\, there will be no hearth or campside cooking demonstration
 s.
DTEND:20260425T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035720Z
DTSTART:20260425T150000Z
GEO:36.029293;-78.975047
LOCATION:Bennett Place State Historic Site
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Uneasy Peace: 161st Anniversary Commemoration
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51958184125172
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/uneasy-peace-161st-anniversary-commemo
 ration
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Lectures & Talks,Panels & Book Discussions
DESCRIPTION:Come hear the exciting life episodes of America’s pioneer hero 
 Daniel Boone during the tumultuous\, eventful years of our Founding Era (17
 73-1783). He takes the initial steps to begin America’s First Westward Move
 ment to create Kentucky and then fights to keep a new nation free. Follow t
 he challenging adventures of this favorite son of North Carolina on the wes
 tern front in rhythm with the Revolution back east.\n\nRandell Jones is an 
 award-winning writer and storyteller\, serving 14 years as an invited membe
 r of the Road Scholar Speaker’s Bureau of the NC Humanities Council and rec
 ipient of the History Award Medal from the National Society\, Daughters of 
 the American Revolution. He is the author of In the Footsteps of Daniel Boo
 ne and Before They Were Heroes at Kings Mountain as well as other books of 
 the pioneer era and the American Revolution. This presentation is illustrat
 ed by scores of images he has captured at historical reenactments during th
 e last 20 years.\n\n"Daniel Boone" is donating $10 from the purchase of eac
 h copy of In the Footsteps of Daniel Boone at this event to the Charlotte M
 useum of History to help us all commemorate and celebrate 250 years of inde
 pendence. Autographed copies are $30\, including sales tax\, so one-third o
 f your purchase benefits everyone who visits Charlotte Museum of History. H
 uzzah!
DTEND:20260425T163000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035720Z
DTSTART:20260425T153000Z
GEO:35.23394;-80.766646
LOCATION:Charlotte Museum of History
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Between Two Sons—Daniel Boone during the American Revolution with R
 andell Jones
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52507111580542
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/between-two-sonsdaniel-boone-during-th
 e-american-revolution-with-randell-jones
END:VEVENT
