BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Performances & Arts,Concerts (Music),Dance
DESCRIPTION:Please note: this event has been rescheduled from March 28 to A
 pril 25.\n\nCelebrate spring with an immersive afternoon of Persian classic
 al and folk music and dance. We have gathered Iranian musicians\, a dancer\
 , and a visual artist from across North America to create a breathtaking jo
 urney through the elegant beauty of Persian art. This performance blends or
 iginal music\, dance\, and visual art to explore the rich and diverse folk 
 traditions from different regions of Iran.\n\nAbout NCMA Sacred Song Series
 \nThis series features music inspired by global faith traditions\, bringing
  to life the diversity of religious expression in our region and the NCMA c
 ollection. Performances include both traditional and contemporary music\, r
 anging from Persian-Jewish piyyut (liturgical poems) to Sufi ragas to Black
  gospel.\n\nProgram\n\nPart 1: Sayeh Ensemble (45 min.)\n• Mahya Hamedi\, v
 ocals\n• Hamed Tabkhi\, tar\n• Pouya Shabanpour\, tonbak/daf\n• Dorsa Davoo
 dabadi\, dance\n• Behzad Riyazi\, visual art\n• Peter Sumner\, cello\n\nInt
 ermission (10–15 min.)\n\nPart 2: Special Guest Performance (30 min.)\nWe a
 re pleased to have a renowned Persian tar player and her husband perform.\n
 • Sahba Motallebi\, tar\n• Reza Mohsenipour\, tar
DTEND:20260425T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035720Z
DTSTART:20260425T193000Z
GEO:35.807856;-78.703922
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Art
SEQUENCE:0
