DESCRIPTION:Starting May 1\, Museum mammalogist Dr. Roland Kays and colleag
 ues will retrace the historic route of Lewis and Clark\, comparing historic
  wildlife observations to what camera traps find today. Along the way\, Kay
 s and company will meet local experts to learn how animal populations have 
 changed over the 250 years of our country’s history. Follow along on the Re
 turn of the Wild website and YouTube channel. You can also join us at the D
 aily Planet Theater (or on the Museum’s YouTube channel) for live check-ins
  with the team at 1pm on May 3\, 10 and 16 as well as 11am on May 28\, June
  4 and June 17.
