BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:
DESCRIPTION:Friends of Lower Haw is offering another outing in its “Take a 
 Walk on the Wild Side” hiking series in the Lower Haw River State Natural A
 rea. We are fortunate to still have some wildness with this amazing natural
  resource running through a growing urbanized area. Join Outdoor NC Guide &
  Haw River native Ben Clarke and his trusty dog Rocco for a spectacular 1.5
  mile round-trip evening hike down the west bank of the Haw from Highway 64
 . We'll pass some of the most famous rapids on the river and lots of native
  mountain laurel\, which should be at the peak of their flowering season! O
 ur hike will take us to Gabriel's Bend\, a Class III rapid where the Haw ha
 s cut a mighty cliff out of the riverbank. The trail climbs this cliff to a
  unique overlook surveying more than a mile of the river! Please be aware t
 hat this hike involves plenty of rock scrabbling\, uneven ground on informa
 l trails\, and the risk of poison ivy\, ticks\, and mosquitos. Sturdy shoes
 \, bug spray\, and water recommended! Friendly dogs on leash are welcome bu
 t may struggle with the terrain. Anyone up for a somewhat challenging but h
 ighly rewarding hike are welcome - no pre-registration required! Contact lo
 werhawevents@gmail.com for questions or to let us know you’re coming.
DTSTAMP:20260508T035722Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260508
GEO:35.730547;-79.107059
LOCATION:US 64 Haw River Canoe Access
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Gabriel's Bend Overlook Hike
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52613212833331
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/gabriels-bend-overlook-hike
END:VEVENT
