BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of the United States’ 250th anniversary\, the As
 heville Choral Society presents Out Of Many\, One\, a thoughtful and richly
  textured concert exploring the many voices that have shaped the nation’s i
 dentity.\n\n\nPerformances will take place May 8 and 9 at Central United Me
 thodist Church.\nDrawing inspiration from the phrase E Pluribus Unum—“out o
 f many\, one”—the program\nweaves together a wide range of musical traditio
 ns\, reflecting the diverse cultural roots\,\nhistories\, and perspectives 
 that continue to define the United States. Through folk songs\,\nspirituals
 \, and contemporary choral works\, the concert invites audiences to conside
 r both the promise of unity and the realities of a shared history that is s
 till unfolding.\nPerformed by a 130-voice chorus known for its professional
 -level sound\, the program balances moments of celebration with opportuniti
 es for reflection.\n\n\nTraditional melodies sit alongside modern compositi
 ons\, offering space to honor resilience\,\nacknowledge struggle\, and reco
 gnize the ongoing work of building a more inclusive and\nequitable society.
 \n\n\nSelections in the program draw from Indigenous\, African American\, A
 ppalachian\, and immigrant musical traditions\, as well as works that speak
  to themes of home\, service\, identity\, and belonging. The result is not 
 a single narrative\, but a musical conversation - one that embraces complex
 ity while pointing toward connection.\n\n\nThe concert also features appear
 ances by Tempus\, the Asheville Choral Society’s select vocal ensemble\, wh
 ose chamber performances add an additional layer of intimacy and nuance to 
 the program.\n\nUnder the direction of Artistic Director and conductor Dr. 
 Melodie Galloway\, the Asheville Choral Society continues to present progra
 ms that are both artistically compelling and culturally resonant.\n\n“This 
 program is an opportunity to reflect on who we are\, and who we are still b
 ecoming\,” said Dr. Galloway. “The idea of E Pluribus Unum is both an aspir
 ation and a challenge. Through this music\, we honor the many voices that h
 ave shaped our shared story - and we hold space for listening\, for underst
 anding\, and for connection.”\n\n\nOut Of Many\, One invites audiences into
  a musical experience that is at once celebratory and contemplative - a rem
 inder that the strength of a chorus\, like that of a nation\, lies not in u
 niformity\, but in the willingness of many voices to come together.
DTEND:20260509T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035722Z
DTSTART:20260509T200000Z
GEO:35.593125;-82.553545
LOCATION:Central United Methodist Church\, Asheville
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Asheville Choral Society presents Out Of Many\, One
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52815657399609
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/asheville-choral-society-presents-out-
 of-many-one-9265
END:VEVENT
