CATEGORIES:Performances & Arts,Education Programs,Lectures & Talks
DESCRIPTION:On the cusp of World War II\, professional artists were commiss
 ioned to design artwork for religious services on military installations\, 
 Naval ships\, and in the field. The Citizens Committee for the Army and Nav
 y answered the call from Chaplains to provide religious symbolic beauty for
  their divine services. The result was an extensive program to provide 3-pi
 ece altar paintings or triptychs. The first one was created for the USS Nor
 th Carolina and lives in the Battleship’s collections. Join us to explore t
 he art\, history\, and spiritual support for all during World War II.\n\nMa
 y 13\, 2026 at 6 PM\nWardroom\, Battleship North Carolina\n1 Battleship Roa
 d\, Wilmington\, NC\n\n$5 in advance\; $8 at the door (as space allows)\nFr
 iends Members: Free\n\nTo purchase tickets\, visit bit.ly/launchingliberty
DTEND:20260513T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035723Z
DTSTART:20260513T220000Z
GEO:34.236158;-77.953643
LOCATION: Battleship North Carolina\, Wardroom
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Triptychs for Victory: Altar Paintings for the American Armed Force
 s in World War II
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52701392040349
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/triptychs-for-victory-altar-paintings-
 for-the-american-armed-forces-in-world-war-ii
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Panels & Book Discussions
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an engaging evening with Michael W. Twitty\, James 
 Beard Award–winning culinary historian\, writer\, and educator. In conversa
 tion with author and UNC professor Marcie Cohen Ferris\, he discusses his l
 atest book\, Recipes from the American South. Through storytelling\, histor
 y\, and food traditions\, they explore the rich connections between cuisine
 \, culture\, faith and identity in the American South and Jewish life.\n\nD
 iscover both iconic dishes and lesser-known specialties from the author of 
 this classic cookbook in the making in a post-talk tasting event.
DTEND:20260513T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035723Z
DTSTART:20260513T223000Z
GEO:35.807856;-78.703922
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Art\, NCMA Cafe
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:An Evening with Michael Twitty
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52702273783798
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/an-evening-with-michael-twitty
END:VEVENT
