BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Workshops & Trainings
DESCRIPTION:Help us kick off our Plott Hound Book Club with a metal stampin
 g bookmark-making workshop and book swap! Grab your previously read books a
 nd head to Adventures in Bloom in downtown Apex for a one-of-a-kind experie
 nce. Your ticket grants you access to both the bookmark workshop and the bo
 ok swap. After crafting your own metal-stamped bookmark\, hang out with oth
 er PHLC readers and pick up any of the books that catch your eye in the swa
 p! Not a PHLC book club member? That’s OK—join us anyway! Beverages and sna
 cks are BYOB. \n\nPlease note: Due to space restrictions\, visitors in grou
 ps should buy multiple tickets simultaneously to guarantee seats together.\
 n\nFree parking is available behind the building next to the train tracks o
 n a first-come\, first-served basis. To learn more about Adventures in Bloo
 m\, visit their website.
DTEND:20260516T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035723Z
DTSTART:20260516T140000Z
GEO:35.731159;-78.851153
LOCATION:Adventures in Bloom
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Metal Stamping Bookmark Workshop and Book Swap
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52631030381603
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/metal-stamping-bookmark-workshop-and-b
 ook-swap
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Exhibits & Tours,Guided Tours,Special Site Pr
 ograms
DESCRIPTION:Join us for “Mountain Mothers\,” a special guided tour at Vance
  Birthplace that looks closely at the experiences of mothers and children i
 n 19th-century Western North Carolina.\n\nExplore the spaces where women li
 ke Mira Vance\, Leah Erwin\, and Elizabeth Hemphill would have had to navig
 ate pregnancy and childbirth as we discuss maternal health and family dynam
 ics in Southern Appalachia in the 1800s. This tour will cover both the joys
  and the dangers of childbearing in an environment shaped by slavery and wa
 r and with limited access to medical resources. Due to the sensitive and di
 fficult nature of some of the topics we will explore\, we recommend this to
 ur for mature audiences only. \n\nRegister via Zeffy to reserve your spot! 
 Tours are offered at 10am and 1pm and will run for approximately 75 minutes
 . Tickets are free for mothers and $5 each otherwise. Spaces are limited\, 
 so claim your spot today! \n\nThis special program is sponsored by the Moun
 tain History and Culture Group. All proceeds go towards supplies and materi
 als for educational programming at Vance Birthplace.
DTEND:20260516T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035723Z
DTSTART:20260516T140000Z
GEO:35.700986;-82.496251
LOCATION:Governor Zebulon B. Vance Birthplace
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Mountain Mothers: A Special Guided Tour at Vance Birthplace
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52709773555586
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/mountain-mothers-a-special-guided-tour
 -at-vance-birthplace
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Youth & Family Activities
DESCRIPTION:The Rootle Roadster Tour will be making a stop at the Potato Fe
 stival on Saturday\, May 16\, from 10 a.m. to 2 p.m. The Museum of the Albe
 marle\, a part of the Division of State History Museums\, Office of Archive
 s and History\, is an agency of the North Carolina Department of Natural an
 d Cultural Resources.\n\nFamilies with children ages 8 and younger will rec
 eive free\, playful learning experiences in their community. The event will
  feature hands-on activities\, educational resources\, and demonstrations b
 y community partners. All activities and takeaways are aligned with literac
 y\, physical\, sensory\, social-emotional\, and STEM curriculum. \n\nThe Ro
 otle Roadster Tour is made possible through the Albemarle Alliance for Chil
 dren and Families.
DTEND:20260516T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035723Z
DTSTART:20260516T140000Z
GEO:36.296532;-76.219757
LOCATION:Museum of the Albemarle
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Rootle Roadster Tour
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52648811154855
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/rootle-roadster-tour
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:March 14 – August 23\, 2026\n\nIn the ultimate battle for survi
 val\, every animal has a plan.\n\nExplore the striking ways nature fights b
 ack in “Staying Alive\,” featuring 17 live animals from around the world wi
 th unbelievable self-defense strategies. Come face to face with trippy toad
 s\, armored armadillos\, a two-toed sloth and more.\n\nDiscover how these d
 efenders deploy an amazing arsenal of high-fashion camouflage and mimicry\,
  specialized armor and advanced chemical warfare – like stink bombs\, caboo
 se cannons and smoke screens – to hide in plain sight\, stand their ground 
 or even drop a limb and make a run for it. Enjoy live animal encounters\, l
 arger-than-life sculptures\, 3D tactile experiences and interactive program
 s.\n\nPerfect for families and animal enthusiasts of all ages. Offered in E
 nglish & Spanish.
DTEND:20260516T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035723Z
DTSTART:20260516T140000Z
GEO:35.782156;-78.639336
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Staying Alive 
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52207082963176
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/staying-alive
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:KMHM is excited to present Women at the Edge of War: Carolina P
 iedmont's Heroines of the American Revolution. This exhibit highlights the 
 daily courage and civic work of women in the Carolinas\, whose efforts were
  essential to Revolutionary resistance and survival on the southern frontie
 r.\n\nThe exhibit will run from Feb. 17\, 2026 to May 30\, 2026. The museum
  is open Tues-Sat\, 10-4. Admission is free. Check out kingsmountainmuseum.
 org or call 704-739-1019 for more information.
DTEND:20260516T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035723Z
DTSTART:20260516T140000Z
GEO:35.239004;-81.342181
LOCATION:Kings Mountain Historical Museum
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Women at the Edge of War: Carolina Piedmont's Heroines of the Ameri
 can Revolution
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51878259898661
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/women-at-the-edge-of-war-carolina-pied
 monts-heroines-of-the-american-revolution
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations,Reenactments & Living History
DESCRIPTION:In May 1771\, an armed band of backcountry farmers known as the
  Regulators clashed with Royal Governor William Tryon’s North Carolina mili
 tia on the very ground now preserved as the Alamance Battleground State His
 toric Site. \n\nThis spring\, join us as we honor the 255th anniversary wit
 h a special reenactment and commemoration. Mark your calendars and stay tun
 ed for details on how you can experience history brought vividly to life.
DTEND:20260516T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035723Z
DTSTART:20260516T150000Z
GEO:36.009795;-79.521351
LOCATION:Alamance Battleground State Historic Site
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY: Battle of Alamance Reenactment: 255th Anniversary Commemoration
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51339822153285
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/battle-of-alamance-reenactment-255th-a
 nniversary-commemoration
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations,Festivals & Fairs
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate five years of fiber arts at the Fifth Annual Fiber Fr
 olic\, held at Hickory Ridge History Museum in Boone\, NC. Fiber\, crafters
 \, and curious families all come together for a full day of hands-on demons
 trations and traditional textile arts.\n\nExplore the craft traditions that
  sustained mountain communities for generations through live demonstrations
  and interactive activities\, including spinning\, wool carding\, weaving\,
  natural dyeing\, and knitting and crocheting. Whether you are a lifelong f
 iber artist or picking up a drop spindle for the very first time\, the Fibe
 r Frolic is a welcoming\, all-ages event with something to discover at ever
 y cabin.\n\nFree admission. All ages welcome. No registration required.
DTEND:20260516T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035723Z
DTSTART:20260516T150000Z
GEO:36.208683;-81.669982
LOCATION:Hickory Ridge History Museum
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Fiber Frolic at Hickory Ridge History Museum
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52461436700238
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/fiber-frolic-at-hickory-ridge-history-
 museum
END:VEVENT
