 es & Talks,Celebrations & Commemorations,Reenactments & Living History
DESCRIPTION:All are invited to a free\, public Screening of The American Co
 nstitution by award winning documentarian David Garrigus. This film chronic
 les the events of the 1787 Constitutional Convention in the Founders’ own w
 ords.\n\nPost screening Q&A led by Dr. George Van Cleve (Harvard JD\; UVA P
 hD)\, preeminent constitutional historian and author.\n\nAdmission is Free\
 ; Donations to NC Sons of the American Revolution Brigade Project welcome.\
 nDoors open at 5:45 PM. 290 seats\, first come\, first seated.\nDoors close
  when full or at 6:45 PM and screening starts immediately thereafter.\n \n\
 nhttps://ncssar.org/event/public-screeningof-the-award-winning-production-t
 he-american-constitution/
DTEND:20260519T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035723Z
DTSTART:20260518T214500Z
GEO:35.867402;-78.54124
LOCATION:Wake Tech Northern Campus Lecture Hall\, Building E
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Public Screening of The American Constitution
