BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Lectures & Talks
DESCRIPTION:What was it like to sail unarmed into a war zone? During World 
 War II\, the civilian sailors of the U.S. Merchant Marine transported troop
 s\, fuel\, and critical supplies through dangerous waters—often under const
 ant threat. This program explores the daily realities\, risks\, and resilie
 nce of the men and women who kept the war effort moving\, bringing to life 
 a vital story that is too often overlooked.\n\nStep aboard with the Battles
 hip’s Executive Director Dr. Jay Martin and explore this remarkable chapter
  of history.\n\nWednesday\, May 20\, 2026 | 6:00 PM\nBattleship North Carol
 ina Wardroom\n1 Battleship Road\, Wilmington\, NC\n\nAdmission:\n$5 advance
  online registration\n$8 at the door\nFriends Members: Free\n\nSpace is lim
 ited! To reserve your spot\, visit bit.ly/merchant-marine
DTEND:20260520T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035723Z
DTSTART:20260520T220000Z
GEO:34.236158;-77.953643
LOCATION: Battleship North Carolina\, Wardroom
SEQUENCE:0
