BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Workshops & Trainings
DESCRIPTION:Help us kick off our Plott Hound Book Club with a metal stampin
 g bookmark-making workshop and book swap! Grab your previously read books a
 nd head to Adventures in Bloom in downtown Apex for a one-of-a-kind experie
 nce. Your ticket grants you access to both the bookmark workshop and the bo
 ok swap. After crafting your own metal-stamped bookmark\, hang out with oth
 er PHLC readers and pick up any of the books that catch your eye in the swa
 p! Not a PHLC book club member? That’s OK—join us anyway! Beverages and sna
 cks are BYOB. \n\nPlease note: Due to space restrictions\, visitors in grou
 ps should buy multiple tickets simultaneously to guarantee seats together.\
 n\nFree parking is available behind the building next to the train tracks o
 n a first-come\, first-served basis. To learn more about Adventures in Bloo
 m\, visit their website.
DTEND:20260529T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035724Z
DTSTART:20260528T223000Z
GEO:35.731159;-78.851153
LOCATION:Adventures in Bloom
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Metal Stamping Bookmark Workshop and Book Swap
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52631090867988
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/metal-stamping-bookmark-workshop-and-b
 ook-swap-4594
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Performances & Arts,Concerts (Music)
DESCRIPTION:Featuring the Joe Alterman Quartet with special guest Christian
  Tamburr\n\nStep into the rich\, interconnected story of American music—whe
 re cultures converge\, boundaries dissolve\, and timeless songs are born. T
 he concert From Irving Berlin to Louis Armstrong celebrates the extraordina
 ry creative exchange between Jewish composers and African American performe
 rs that helped define the sound of the 20th century. These collaborations d
 idn’t just produce hit songs—they built the foundations of jazz\, Broadway\
 , and the Great American Songbook.\n\nFeaturing renowned internationally to
 uring jazz pianist Joe Alterman and his quartet\, this unforgettable concer
 t brings new life to beloved classics with energy\, authenticity\, and hear
 t. Joining the ensemble on vibraphone is special guest Christian Tamburr\, 
 whose artistry and versatility add a vibrant dimension to this musical jour
 ney. Together\, they explore iconic works by legendary figures such as Irvi
 ng Berlin\, George Gershwin\, Duke Ellington\, and Louis Armstrong\, tracin
 g the evolution of a uniquely American sound rooted in shared influence and
  mutual inspiration. This is more than a concert—it’s a celebration of cult
 ural collaboration\, musical innovation\, and the enduring power of song.
DTEND:20260529T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035724Z
DTSTART:20260528T230000Z
GEO:35.807856;-78.703922
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Art\, SECU Auditorium
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:From Irving Berlin to Louis Armstrong: Celebrating the Jewish Songw
 riters and African American Performers Who Shaped American Music
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52711235576495
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/from-irving-berlin-to-louis-armstrong-
 celebrating-the-jewish-songwriters-and-african-american-performers-who-shap
 ed-american-music
END:VEVENT
