BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:March 14 – August 23\, 2026\n\nIn the ultimate battle for survi
 val\, every animal has a plan.\n\nExplore the striking ways nature fights b
 ack in “Staying Alive\,” featuring 17 live animals from around the world wi
 th unbelievable self-defense strategies. Come face to face with trippy toad
 s\, armored armadillos\, a two-toed sloth and more.\n\nDiscover how these d
 efenders deploy an amazing arsenal of high-fashion camouflage and mimicry\,
  specialized armor and advanced chemical warfare – like stink bombs\, caboo
 se cannons and smoke screens – to hide in plain sight\, stand their ground 
 or even drop a limb and make a run for it. Enjoy live animal encounters\, l
 arger-than-life sculptures\, 3D tactile experiences and interactive program
 s.\n\nPerfect for families and animal enthusiasts of all ages. Offered in E
 nglish & Spanish.
DTEND:20260529T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035724Z
DTSTART:20260529T140000Z
GEO:35.782156;-78.639336
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Staying Alive 
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52207082973427
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/staying-alive
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:KMHM is excited to present Women at the Edge of War: Carolina P
 iedmont's Heroines of the American Revolution. This exhibit highlights the 
 daily courage and civic work of women in the Carolinas\, whose efforts were
  essential to Revolutionary resistance and survival on the southern frontie
 r.\n\nThe exhibit will run from Feb. 17\, 2026 to May 30\, 2026. The museum
  is open Tues-Sat\, 10-4. Admission is free. Check out kingsmountainmuseum.
 org or call 704-739-1019 for more information.
DTEND:20260529T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035724Z
DTSTART:20260529T140000Z
GEO:35.239004;-81.342181
LOCATION:Kings Mountain Historical Museum
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Women at the Edge of War: Carolina Piedmont's Heroines of the Ameri
 can Revolution
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51878259910958
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/women-at-the-edge-of-war-carolina-pied
 monts-heroines-of-the-american-revolution
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Homeschool & Education Days,Youth & Family Ac
 tivities
DESCRIPTION:Homeschool Day is back at the Charlotte Museum of History! Join
  us for a special day designed just for homeschool families\, with hands-on
  activities\, crafts\, and interactive experiences that bring Charlotte’s h
 istory to life.\n\nThroughout the historic homesite\, families can explore 
 a variety of activity tables created especially for students in grades 3–6.
  Young historians can try their hand at:\n\nTextile production by making a 
 mini loom and learning how to weave\n\nWater filtration at the historic Spr
 inghouse by building a filter using natural materials\n\nQuill and ink writ
 ing and discover how important documents in our nation’s history were creat
 ed\n\nPrinting and the printing press by making a stamp and creating a prin
 t of their own\n\nRevolutionary War spy communication by writing with invis
 ible ink and decoding messages using the Culper Spy Ring Code\n\n…and more!
 \n\nFamilies will also have the opportunity to explore our newest exhibit\,
  The American Revolution: The Augmented Exhibition\, an immersive and inter
 active experience that uses HistoPads to bring Revolutionary War stories to
  life through augmented reality. This exhibit is especially great for middl
 e and high school students\, but younger learners will enjoy it too. To hel
 p students engage at their own level\, we’ll have companion activity bookle
 ts for elementary\, middle\, and high school ages available while they expl
 ore.\n\nWhether your students love hands-on learning\, local history\, or i
 nteractive technology\, Homeschool Day offers something for the whole famil
 y!
DTEND:20260529T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035724Z
DTSTART:20260529T150000Z
GEO:35.23394;-80.766646
LOCATION:Charlotte Museum of History
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Homeschool Day 2026
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52773217787739
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/homeschool-day-2026
END:VEVENT
