BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Guided Tours,Outdoor & Recreation,Nature & Wild
 life Programs
DESCRIPTION:Join staff from the Library of North Carolina’s Government and 
 Heritage Library and the NC Museum of Natural Sciences for a Native Plant W
 alk focusing on gardening with native plants to attract and support birds.\
 n\nThis plant walk will explore native plantings in the NC Department of Na
 tural and Cultural Resources’ Native Plant Meadow and the NC Museum of Natu
 ral Science’s Native Plant Garden. The event will take place primarily outd
 oors\, with participants traveling approximately ½ mile round-trip via pave
 d sidewalks.\n\nRegistration is requested at slnc.info/plantwalk526.\n\nThi
 s event is hosted in connection with the GHL's Native Plant Seed Library. L
 earn more about our seed library at slnc.info/seeds\, and more about seed l
 ibraries and native plants on our GHL Seed Library Research Guide at slnc.i
 nfo/seedlibraryguide. \n\nQuestions about this event? Contact us at ghl.inf
 o@dncr.nc.gov.
