BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Performances & Arts
DESCRIPTION:Dive into the stories and drama behind The American Constitutio
 n film & the unsung delegates who crafted a document that changed the world
 ! This event is free of charge and the director\, David Garrigus\, will be 
 on hand to answer questions after the showing.\n\nExperience the groundbrea
 king film that unveils the Constitution's dramatic creation. Set in 1787 Ph
 iladelphia\, "The American Constitution" features a stellar cast of actors 
 who bring the framers to life. Best-selling authors and leading historians 
 masterfully reveal how George Washington\, James Madison\, Alexander Hamilt
 on\, Benjamin Franklin and a cadre of unsung delegates crafted a document t
 hat changed the world. The filmmaker\, David Garrigus\, the award-winning f
 ilmmaker behind the PBS critically-acclaimed " Kitty Hawk\; The Wright Brot
 hers' Journey of Invention\," will be on hand to engage in discussion and q
 uestions.\n\nDr. Harry Watson\, retired history professor\, UNC-Chapel Hill
 \, will speak to North Carolina's role in signing the Constitution before t
 he film.\n\nComplimentary refreshments will be served after the screening b
 y the Moyock Woman's Club.
DTEND:20260531T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035725Z
DTSTART:20260531T180000Z
GEO:36.374283;-75.965499
LOCATION:Currituck County Middle School\, Auditorium
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The American Constitution Documentary Film Showing
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52639419877219
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/the-american-constitution-documentary-
 film-showing
END:VEVENT
