BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Workshops & Trainings
DESCRIPTION:Attention Educators! NC History Day invites you to apply for Na
 tional History Day® (NHD) latest iteration of its Historical Argumentation:
  Using Library of Congress Resources to Build a Historical Argument\, Explo
 ring Innovation: Impact\, Influence\, Change in History webinar series. \n\
 nSponsored by the Library of Congress\, this online professional developmen
 t series is designed to deepen participants’ understanding of historical ar
 gumentation and to provide educators with resources and strategies for thei
 r classrooms. The webinar series will run from late July 2026 to November 2
 026 and educators may earn 90 professional development hours or three gradu
 ate extension credits at no cost.\n\nThroughout this series\, educators wil
 l build their knowledge of teaching with online Library of Congress resourc
 es\, complete assignments\, and join monthly webinars. Once complete\, educ
 ators will have demonstrated the ability to share key strategies for resear
 ching\, supporting\, and presenting historical arguments bolstered by prima
 ry sources held by the Library of Congress. Apply here by June 12th.
DTSTAMP:20260508T035728Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260612
LOCATION:
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Teaching Historical Argumentation Webinar Series: Using Library of 
 Congress Resources to Build a Historical Argument\, Exploring Innovation: I
 mpact\, Influence\, Change in History 
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52804523853658
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/teacher-historical-argumentation-webin
 ar-series-using-library-of-congress-resources-to-build-a-historical-argumen
 t-exploring-innovation-impact-influence-change-in-history
END:VEVENT
