BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Juneteenth\, the Battleship North Carolina wi
 ll be illuminated in red\, white\, and blue\, honoring the end of slavery i
 n the United States and celebrating African American freedom\, resilience\,
  and culture.\n\nBeginning at sunset (around 8:30 pm)\, the Battleship’s st
 riking display will cast a glow across the Wilmington skyline—inviting resi
 dents and visitors to pause\, reflect\, and gather in recognition of this i
 mportant date in American history. The illumination will be visible from do
 wntown Wilmington’s Riverwalk\, nearby parks\, and across the Cape Fear Riv
 er.\n\nAs North Carolina’s official World War II memorial\, the Battleship 
 serves as a place for remembrance\, education\, and connection. This specia
 l illumination offers an opportunity for the community to come together in 
 reflection—acknowledging the past while looking ahead with purpose and unde
 rstanding.
DTEND:20260620T013000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035729Z
DTSTART:20260620T003000Z
GEO:34.236158;-77.953643
LOCATION: Battleship North Carolina
