BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Performances & Arts,Education Programs,Workshops & Trainings
DESCRIPTION:Join teaching artist Kimberley Pierce Cartwright for a hand sew
 ing art quilt workshop\, inspired by the African American history\, landsca
 pes\, and textures of Historic Stagville. \n\nIn this class you will learn 
 how to use your fabric stash to put together a complete art project in a fe
 w hours start to finish. We’ll brainstorm designs to create together\, make
  our own patterns and hand-sew art quilt projects. We’ll talk about composi
 tion and color\; visit the landscape and artifacts of Stagville\; and each 
 student will design an 8 x 10 art quilt that can be framed.\n\nThis is a 2.
 5 hour class.\n\nRegistration required. The registration link will be avail
 able by May 15 on this event page.\n\nAbout the artist: Kimberley Pierce Ca
 rtwright was born in Hallsboro\, NC. She began quilting and painting in the
  summer of 2006. Her work evokes emotion through her distinctive use of col
 or. She specializes in small quilt fabric post cards. She’s a member of the
  African American Quilt Circle of Durham and has taught classes in quilting
  and sewing.  Kimberley holds a bachelor of arts degree from Shaw Universit
 y in Radio Television and Film. She also earned a master’s degree in Public
  Affairs Reporting from the University of Illinois at Springfield. \n\n \n\
 nImage credit to Quiltfolk\, photography by Azuree Wiitala.
DTEND:20260620T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035729Z
DTSTART:20260620T163000Z
GEO:36.115365;-78.841527
LOCATION:Historic Stagville\, Visitors Center
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Juneteenth Art Quilt Workshop - Historic Stagville
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52763877784014
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/juneteenth-art-quilt-workshop-historic
 -stagville
END:VEVENT
