BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Lectures & Talks
DESCRIPTION:Its that time of year again! Come celebrate the summer at Merch
 ants Millpond State Park with our 4th year of the Summer Junior Adventure S
 eries! In this series\, we have a different topic that we teach about every
  Monday at 10 AM throughout the summer. \n\nThis week its all about camping
 ! Everyone loves camping\, but not many people know how to plan and pack fo
 r it. Join us as we cover what supplies you'll need to camp\, skills needed
 \, and  best practices. If you've ever had any questions about camping or g
 ear\, then this is program you've been waiting for!\n\nThis program will st
 art promptly at 10 AM at the visitor center. Guests are encouraged to dress
  for the weather as part of this program will be outside.
DTEND:20260622T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035730Z
DTSTART:20260622T140000Z
GEO:36.437278;-76.701271
LOCATION:Merchants Millpond State Park\, Visitor Center
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Ranger Jeffrey's Camping 101 - Summer Junior Adventure Series
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52602520473263
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/ranger-jeffreys-camping-101-summer-jun
 ior-adventure-series
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Performances & Arts,Concerts (Music)
DESCRIPTION:Amplifying diverse Appalachian voices\n\nMusic and dance have b
 een a vital part of the Folk School since its founding in 1925. As we celeb
 rate our 100th year\, Centennial Sounds honors this legacy by spotlighting 
 the cultural richness of Appalachian music and the many voices that shape i
 t. This special performance series will feature five headliners whose work 
 expands and redefines the story of Appalachian music. Through these concert
 s\, we aim to create new opportunities for our community in Western North C
 arolina to experience the full spectrum of Appalachian sound.\n\nThe Folk S
 chool is supported by the North Carolina Arts Council\, a division of the D
 epartment of Natural and Cultural Resources.
DTEND:20260623T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035730Z
DTSTART:20260622T230000Z
GEO:35.03748;-83.964153
LOCATION:Folk School Festival Barn
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Centennial Sounds
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52737194653684
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/centennial-sounds-821
END:VEVENT
