BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Outdoor & Recreation,Outdoor Recreation (kaya
 k, paddle, hikes),Nature & Wildlife Programs,Youth & Family Activities
DESCRIPTION:In honor of National Pollinator Week\, join a ranger at Boone F
 ork Parking Area (milepost 299.9 on the Blue Ridge Parkway) for a wildflowe
 r and pollinator ID hike along the Upper Boone Fork Trail. Learn how to ID 
 some common blooming wildflower species of the high country\, and some loca
 l pollinator species that keep those flowers blooming every year. \n\nThis 
 1.5 mile easy hike does have some tree roots and rocks to walk over\, so pl
 ease wear appropriate hiking shoes and dress for the weather.\n\nThere are 
 no bathrooms at Boone Fork Parking Area.
DTEND:20260624T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035730Z
DTSTART:20260624T170000Z
LOCATION:Boone Fork Parking Area
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Wildflower & Pollinator ID Hike
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51833340502333
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/wildflower-pollinator-id-hike
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
DESCRIPTION:This program honors Evelyn Pope by reading books. \n\nEvelyn\, 
 a college librarian born in 1908 and died in 1995\, loved a variety of book
 s from The Adventures of Tom Sawyer to Shakespeare and James Baldwin. The p
 rogram brings community members together monthly at the museum to discuss b
 ooks\, focusing on works by Black writers or featuring Black subjects\, inc
 luding fiction and non-fiction. Discussions will use questions to facilitat
 e conversation.\n\n"Mama Day" by Gloria Naylor\nWednesday\, Feb. 25\n "The 
 Black Angels: The Untold Story of the Nurses Who Helped Cure Tuberculosis" 
 by Maria Smilios\nWednesday\, April 22\n "A Visitation of Spirits" by Randa
 ll Kenan\nWednesday\, June 24\n "Becoming Lunsford Lane: The Lives of an Am
 erican Aeneas" by Craig Friend\nWednesday\, Aug. 26\n "Ring Shout" by P. De
 jeli Clark\nThursday\, Oct. 29Registration opens Jan. 23.  An optional book
  bundle will be available to purchase at registration. Books can be picked 
 up at the Dr. M.T. Pope House Museum.
DTEND:20260625T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035730Z
DTSTART:20260624T223000Z
GEO:35.77372;-78.638254
LOCATION:Dr. M.T. Pope House Museum
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Dr. M.T. Pope House Presents: Evelyn's Book Club
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51886320481218
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/dr-mt-pope-house-presents-evelyns-book
 -club
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
DESCRIPTION:Pretend you’ve been recruited as a member of the Culper Spy Rin
 g\, and you need to know how to decipher a message written in invisible ink
 . Supplies include a paint brush\, water\, drying cloth\, vitriol (diluted 
 sulfuric acid)\, Thomas Jefferson cipher and “furnace box.” Read the clues 
 to find the coin with a hidden message\, reveal the message using the brush
  and vitriol\, then use the cipher to decode the message.\n\nContact: Nancy
  Locquet Absillis\, nancy.locquet@naturalsciences.org
DTSTAMP:20260508T035730Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260625
GEO:35.782156;-78.639336
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
