UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52504709668559
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/spy-training-101-decode-a-secret-messa
 ge
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:May 2–August 9\, 2026\n\nEast Building\, Level B\, Meymandi Exh
 ibition Gallery\n\nKnowing the West embraces and reexamines perceptions of 
 the American West to create more inclusive and complex dialogues. The exhib
 ition reflects the diverse perspectives that have contributed to art and li
 fe in the region. Presenting Native American works together with art by non
 -Native makers\, it reveals how the stories we tell and the visual language
  we employ influence understanding of our nation’s history and cultures.
DTSTAMP:20260508T035730Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260625
GEO:35.807856;-78.703922
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Art
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Knowing the West
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52702202757316
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/knowing-the-west
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
DESCRIPTION:The 2026 Second Annual Memorial Pop Top Checkers Tournament\, t
 o be held June 25-27\, 2026 will attract players from all over the region. 
  Held in the charming town of Waxhaw. NC\, the tournament offers not only a
  change to compete but also an opportunity to explore the rich history of t
 his historical location.  \n\nParticipants and spectators alike can enjoy a
  weedend filled with checkers while experiencing the culture\, history and 
 charm that is historic Waxhaw\, North Carolina.  Whether you're a seasoned 
 player or a curios newcomer\, the tournament promises an unforgettable expe
 rience for everyone.\n\nFor more information visit www.poptopcheckers.com
DTSTAMP:20260508T035730Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260625
GEO:34.924604;-80.742522
LOCATION:Waxhaw Woman's Club
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:W.H. Collins/Maxwell McCain 2nd Annual Memorial "Pop Top" Checkers 
 Tournament
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52691257719760
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/wh-collinsmaxwell-mccain-2nd-annual-me
 morial-pop-top-checkers-tournament
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Homeschool & Education Days,Exhibits & Tours,
 Special Site Programs,Outdoor & Recreation,Outdoor Recreation (kayak, paddl
 e, hikes),Nature & Wildlife Programs,Youth & Family Activities
DESCRIPTION:Join the Curious Minds Adventure Scavenger Hunt at Elk Knob Sta
 te Park. Journey through northern hardwood forest\, follow winding mountain
  trails\, and explore the unique ecosystems of this high-elevation park. Ke
 ep your eyes open—what signs of wildlife or weather-shaped landscapes will 
 you uncover? Look for unique rocks that make Elk Knob a very special clue i
 n North Carolina’s geologic history. Start at the Visitor Center and scan t
 he QR code in your Actionbound app. Flyers with the QR code will be placed 
 in the Park Office and on all park map kiosks. \n\nThe adventures are avail
 able on the Actionbound app – a free download to your cellphone through you
 r phone’s app store. There’s no need to create a profile and no personal da
 ta is collected with Actionbound. You simply find new hunts by searching fo
 r the park name or scanning the associated QR code posted for your park’s a
 dventure.\n\nThis program is made possible through a partnership with the N
 C Science Trail (ncsciencetrail.org)! Visit their website for more Curious 
 Minds Adventure Scavenger Hunts being held in other NC State Parks and for 
 other programs being offered throughout the state. \n\nThis scavenger hunt 
 is running now through August 31\, 2026.
DTEND:20260626T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035730Z
DTSTART:20260625T110000Z
GEO:36.333462;-81.696432
LOCATION:Elk Knob State Park
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Elk Knob State Park: Curious Minds Adventure Scavenger Hunt
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52745325273564
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/elk-knob-state-park-curious-minds-adve
 nture-scavenger-hunt
END:VEVENT
