DESCRIPTION:This Independence Day\, celebrate America's 250 with a guided h
 ike that brings local history to life through the lens of our living landma
 rks: witness trees. Participants will learn how to identify and age several
  species of trees along the Piedmont Loop Trail\, trees which served as sil
 ent observers to events of the past and to the history being made each day.
 \n\nTrail distance is 1.4 miles\, "easy" but traveling over some short\, st
 eeper inclines. Bring what you need to be comfortable\, dress for the weath
 er\, and please wear close-toed walking shoes (for stepping short distances
  off trail to measure trees). Recommended for adults and youth ages five an
 d older. Registration suggested but not required.
DTEND:20260704T150000Z
