 ns
DESCRIPTION:Join Salem Band for an All-American band concert in the town Sq
 uare\, our Annual Stars & Stripes performance honoring veterans in our comm
 unity with marches\, big bands\, sing-alongs\, Armed Forces Salute\, and of
  course\, Star & Stripes Forever! Hear two World Premieres of original comp
 ositions celebrating our nation’s 250th Anniversary and the original Indepe
 ndence Day celebration in Salem Square: Healthy\, Wealthy\, and Wise by Ste
 ven Sherrill\; and American Hussite by David Mailman. The program includes 
 Tchaikovsky’s 1812 Overture\, Places USA\, and Cosmopolitan America. Don’t 
 miss the sibling vocal duo featuring our own SB vocalist Mignon Dobbins and
  brother David Dobbins\, baritone – singing\, song-leading\, and narrating.
   Arrive at 6:45 pm to enjoy pre-concert jazz by The Luke Childress Quartet
 . This event is generously supported by a grant from The Winston-Salem Foun
 dation.\n\nFREE in Salem Square\, Old Salem\, Winston-Salem. Bring a lawn c
 hair or blanket and a picnic. Rain-date = Sunday\, July 05.\n\nEstablished 
 in 1771\, Salem Band is the oldest\, continuous mixed wind ensemble in the 
 nation. Eileen Young\, Music Director. \n\nwww.salemband.org \n\nhttps://ww
 w.facebook.com/SalemBandFan/
DTEND:20260705T011500Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035732Z
DTSTART:20260704T233000Z
GEO:36.087131;-80.241844
LOCATION:Salem Square\, Old Salem
