BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations,Reenactments & Living History
DESCRIPTION:250 years ago today\, the “Declaration of Independence” was fir
 st read aloud to the public! Learn about the importance of this document an
 d try your hand at writing like the Founding Fathers. Practice your penmans
 hip with quills and ink provided by our costumed interpreters. FREE. All ag
 es welcome. Drop-in.
DTEND:20260711T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035732Z
DTSTART:20260711T140000Z
GEO:35.979741;-79.992174
LOCATION:High Point Museum
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Quill Pen Writing in the Historical Park
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51825895453250
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/quill-pen-writing-in-the-historical-pa
 rk
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:March 14 – August 23\, 2026\n\nIn the ultimate battle for survi
 val\, every animal has a plan.\n\nExplore the striking ways nature fights b
 ack in “Staying Alive\,” featuring 17 live animals from around the world wi
 th unbelievable self-defense strategies. Come face to face with trippy toad
 s\, armored armadillos\, a two-toed sloth and more.\n\nDiscover how these d
 efenders deploy an amazing arsenal of high-fashion camouflage and mimicry\,
  specialized armor and advanced chemical warfare – like stink bombs\, caboo
 se cannons and smoke screens – to hide in plain sight\, stand their ground 
 or even drop a limb and make a run for it. Enjoy live animal encounters\, l
 arger-than-life sculptures\, 3D tactile experiences and interactive program
 s.\n\nPerfect for families and animal enthusiasts of all ages. Offered in E
 nglish & Spanish.
DTEND:20260711T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035732Z
DTSTART:20260711T140000Z
GEO:35.782156;-78.639336
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Staying Alive 
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52207083008280
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/staying-alive
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
DESCRIPTION:Learn about one of the small arms (musket\, flintlock\, or rifl
 e) that a soldier stationed at Fort Macon would have carried and used.\n\nT
 his will include a blank firing demonstration of the weapon.\nMeet in the f
 ort parade ground.\n\n \n\nPhoto by Jairus Hill : Living historian demonstr
 ating a musket at Fort Macon State Park.
DTEND:20260711T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035732Z
DTSTART:20260711T143000Z
GEO:34.696366;-76.684506
LOCATION:Fort Macon State Park
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Small Arms Demonstration 10:30am & 2:30pm
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52019009718808
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/small-arms-demonstration-1030am-230pm
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Youth & Family Activities
DESCRIPTION:It's America's 250th birthday - celebrate with America250 trivi
 a!\n\nQuestions will be drawn from the US Citizenship test\, as well as his
 tory\, geography\, and pop culture. \n\nFamily Trivia is an all ages event\
 , but these questions will be most appropriate for rising 4th graders and u
 p. Teams of up to five are encouraged (and it's a good idea to have a multi
 ple generations on your team). No team no problem you can form one at the l
 ibrary or go solo!\n\nWinners will get bragging rights (and a prize). \n\nR
 egistration is required. A minimum of five players are needed. The event wi
 ll be canceled if fewer than five people register before registration close
 s.
DTEND:20260711T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035732Z
DTSTART:20260711T180000Z
GEO:34.23293;-77.828256
LOCATION:Northeast Library\, Oak Room
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Family Trivia: America 250 at Northeast Library
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52817321036820
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/family-trivia-america-250-at-northeast
 -library
END:VEVENT
