BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Youth & Family Activities
DESCRIPTION:Discover the historical and natural maritime heritage of northe
 astern North Carolina. Learn about pirates\, lighthouses\, underwater archa
 eology\, watersports\, and aquatic animals as you engage in hands-on activi
 ties and meet with experts.\n\nPreregistration required for groups of 10 or
  more.
DTEND:20260715T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035733Z
DTSTART:20260715T140000Z
GEO:36.296532;-76.219757
LOCATION:Museum of the Albemarle
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Summer Fun Day: Maritime Heritage Day
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52806665237074
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/summer-fun-day-maritime-heritage-day
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations,Reenactments & Living History
DESCRIPTION:Learn about one of the small arms (musket\, flintlock\, or rifl
 e) that a soldier stationed at Fort Macon would have carried and used.\n\nT
 his will include a blank firing demonstration of the weapon.\nMeet in the f
 ort parade ground.\n\n \n\nPhoto by Jairus Hill : Living historian demonstr
 ating a musket at Fort Macon State Park.
DTEND:20260715T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035733Z
DTSTART:20260715T143000Z
GEO:34.696366;-76.684506
LOCATION:Fort Macon State Park\, Fort Parade Ground
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Small Arms Demonstration
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51922179182794
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/small-arms-demonstration-6298
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Lectures & Talks
DESCRIPTION:Andrew Duppstadt\, education and interpretation supervisor for 
 the North Carolina Division of State Historic Sites\, will highlight some o
 f North Carolina’s most famous (or infamous) seafaring personalities\, pira
 tes\, privateers\, and commerce raiders. The presentation explores over 150
  years of maritime history\, including Sir Walter Raleigh\, the Golden Age 
 of Piracy\, the American Revolution\, the War of 1812\, and the American Ci
 vil War.
DTEND:20260715T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035733Z
DTSTART:20260715T160000Z
GEO:36.296532;-76.219757
LOCATION:Museum of the Albemarle\, Gaither Auditorium
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:History for Lunch: “A Highly Planned and Cooperative Form of Theft:
 ” North Carolina’s Naval Raiders\, 1700–1865
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52806721155441
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/history-for-lunch-a-highly-planned-and
 -cooperative-form-of-theft-north-carolinas-naval-raiders-17001865
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation,Outdoor Recreation (kayak, paddle, hikes),N
 ature & Wildlife Programs,Education Programs,Youth & Family Activities
DESCRIPTION:Join us as we hike down to Otter Falls (1.2 miles round trip) t
 o learn about how living and non-living things interact in mountain streams
 . What are all of those insects and other critters swimming and crawling th
 rough the creek? We will catch and identify what type of creature they are 
 and what these species could tell us about water quality. Nets will be prov
 ided. Any participants wanting to get into the stream should bring clothes 
 and shoes that can get wet and a towel to dry off. Make sure to bring water
  for the hike! No pets please. This is a Ranger Workshop with The Town of S
 even Devils.
DTEND:20260715T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035733Z
DTSTART:20260715T170000Z
GEO:36.149669;-81.808644
LOCATION:Otter Falls Trail
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Ranger Workshop - Stream Ecology
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51815547918503
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/ranger-workshop-stream-ecology
END:VEVENT
