CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Workshops & Trainings,Outdoor & Recreation,Ou
 tdoor Recreation (kayak, paddle, hikes)
DESCRIPTION:Registration required at Go Outdoors website: North Carolina WR
 C License - View Event. This workshop is open to those 16 years and older. 
 All minors must be accompanied by an adult.\n\nAre you ready to dive into f
 ly-fishing but don’t know where to start? Join our ‘Before the Cast’ progra
 m and learn everything you need to confidently gear up for your next fishin
 g adventure!\n\nThis hands-on\, interactive class is perfect for beginners 
 and anyone looking to refine their understanding of fly-fishing gear. We’ll
  break down the fundamentals of selecting\, assembling\, and maintaining th
 e right equipment so you can fish effectively and enjoyably.
DTEND:20260719T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035733Z
DTSTART:20260719T140000Z
GEO:36.250909;-79.756467
LOCATION:Haw River State Park\, Main Lodge at 339 Conference Center Drive\,
  Browns Summit\, NC 27214
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Learn to Fly-Fish NC: Before the Cast
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51943186301820
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/learn-to-fly-fish-nc-before-the-cast
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:March 14 – August 23\, 2026\n\nIn the ultimate battle for survi
 val\, every animal has a plan.\n\nExplore the striking ways nature fights b
 ack in “Staying Alive\,” featuring 17 live animals from around the world wi
 th unbelievable self-defense strategies. Come face to face with trippy toad
 s\, armored armadillos\, a two-toed sloth and more.\n\nDiscover how these d
 efenders deploy an amazing arsenal of high-fashion camouflage and mimicry\,
  specialized armor and advanced chemical warfare – like stink bombs\, caboo
 se cannons and smoke screens – to hide in plain sight\, stand their ground 
 or even drop a limb and make a run for it. Enjoy live animal encounters\, l
 arger-than-life sculptures\, 3D tactile experiences and interactive program
 s.\n\nPerfect for families and animal enthusiasts of all ages. Offered in E
 nglish & Spanish.
DTEND:20260719T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035733Z
DTSTART:20260719T140000Z
GEO:35.782156;-78.639336
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Staying Alive 
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52207083014431
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/staying-alive
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
DESCRIPTION:Learn about one of the small arms (musket\, flintlock\, or rifl
 e) that a soldier stationed at Fort Macon would have carried and used.\n\nT
 his will include a blank firing demonstration of the weapon.\nMeet in the f
 ort parade ground.\n\n \n\nPhoto by Jairus Hill : Living historian demonstr
 ating a musket at Fort Macon State Park.
DTEND:20260719T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035733Z
DTSTART:20260719T143000Z
GEO:34.696366;-76.684506
LOCATION:Fort Macon State Park
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Small Arms Demonstration 10:30am & 2:30pm
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52019009721883
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/small-arms-demonstration-1030am-230pm
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Workshops & Trainings,Outdoor & Recreation,Ou
 tdoor Recreation (kayak, paddle, hikes)
DESCRIPTION:Registration Required at Go Outdoors website: North Carolina WR
 C License - View Event. It is recommended to attend 'Learn to Fly-Fish: Bef
 ore the Cast' prior to the this program (10am-12pm same date/location). Thi
 s workshop is open to those 16 years and older. All minors must be accompan
 ied by an adult.\n\nJoin in and learn the basic principles of fly-casting! 
 This hands-on session is perfect for beginners or those looking to refine t
 heir skills. We'll cover essential techniques such as the basic overhead ca
 st\, roll cast\, and line management\, while gaining insights into proper f
 orm and equipment use. This class provides guidance to help you build confi
 dence and enjoy the art of fly fishing. All equipment is provided\, so just
  bring your enthusiasm and get ready to cast without worry!
DTEND:20260719T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035733Z
DTSTART:20260719T170000Z
GEO:36.250909;-79.756467
LOCATION:Haw River State Park\, Main Lodge at 339 Conference Center Drive\,
  Browns Summit\, NC 27214
SEQUENCE:0
