BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Workshops & Trainings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, July 27th\, 2026 | 10am - 3pm\nMountain Gateway Museum
 \n78-C Catawba Avenue\, Old Fort\, NC\, 28762\n\nApply here! Applications c
 lose on Tuesday\, May 26th\, 2026.\n\n\n***Attending middle grades teachers
  will receive $100 stipend + Lunch + .5 CEUs -- Open to middle grades teach
 ers in McDowell\, Burke\, Mitchell\, Yancey\, Rutherford\, and Madison Coun
 ties. \nJoin the North Carolina Department of Natural and Cultural Resource
 s (DNCR) for an exclusive afternoon for area middle-grades educators at Mou
 ntain Gateway Museum!\n\nThe Mountain Gateway Museum explores and celebrate
 s the cultural history of Western North Carolina\, an area spanning 38 coun
 ties from the Blue Ridge Mountains to the Piedmont. When visiting the museu
 m or utilizing it's resources\, students will experience the Southern Appal
 achian past and learn about the people and culture that shaped the western 
 region of North Carolina. \n\nAttending educators  will preview the various
  on-sight activities that can be offered and tailored for visiting school g
 roups\, as well as classroom outreach opportunities. Time will also be prov
 ided for attending teaches to share feedback\, ideas and requests regarding
  what else you would like our site to offer in support of classroom learnin
 g. Attendees will also receive information about DNCR resources for educato
 rs.\n\nAttending educators will also receive:\n\nA $100 stipend (upon compl
 etion of a post-event survey)Lunch.5 CEUsThe chance to network with other e
 ducators from multiple schools across the district\, as well as the opportu
 nity to engage with DNCR/Mountain Gateway Museum staff ready to serve as a 
 source of support for your important work in the classroom!Priority registr
 ation will be given to middle school teachers in McDowell\, Burke\, Mitchel
 l\, Yancey\, Rutherford\, Madison\, & surrounding counties but any K-12 tea
 cher is eligible to apply. (Make sure your distance from the Museum allows 
 you to comfortably arrive by 10 am). Don’t miss the opportunity to experien
 ce what the Mountain Gateway Museum has to offer\, while also enjoying food
  and fellowship with amazing teaching colleagues from across the region! \n
 Please note that late arrivals and early departures cannot be accommodated.
  Before submitting an application\, please check your schedule to ensure yo
 u can arrive by 10:00am and that you are able to stay until 3:00pm\n\nSpace
  is limited to 20 registrants\; filling out this form does not guarantee yo
 ur registration. Participants will be registered based on a combination of 
 ensuring a diversity of schools and grade levels represented\; the order in
  which your application was received per school\; and your application resp
 onses and completeness. You should receive a response to your application n
 o later than May 29th. If after May 29th you have not received a response a
 nd a message is not in your junk/spam folder\, please contact us at educati
 onoutreach@dncr.nc.gov.\n\nCANCELLATION POLICY\nDNCR is committed to provid
 ing free professional development to teachers\, with not even a small fee o
 r deposit required. However\, these programs are costly to the organizers/f
 unders. Thus\, if you receive a space in this event and you find that you n
 eed to cancel at any point\, it is critical to let us know immediately and 
 no later than five days before the event by e-mailing educationoutreach@dnc
 r.nc.gov. Last minute cancellations and "no-shows" with no communication re
 sult in waste of budget\, food\, materials\, etc.\, and prevents wait liste
 d teachers from participating. Except in the case of an emergency\, if a re
 gistered teacher does not show up or communicate no longer being able to at
 tend\, your school may be billed for a $75 no-show fee.\n\nQuestions?\n\nCo
 ntact us at educationoutreach@dncr.nc.gov\n\n \n\nThis event is funded and 
 hosted by North Carolina Department of Natural and Cultural Resources (DNCR
 ) and Friends of the Mountain Gateway Museum.
DTEND:20260727T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035733Z
DTSTART:20260727T140000Z
GEO:35.627587;-82.180647
LOCATION:Mountain Gateway Museum and Heritage Center
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Educator Workshop: Hands-On History at the Mountain Gateway Museum 
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52630107404110
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/mgmteacherworkshop
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Performances & Arts,Concerts (Music)
DESCRIPTION:Amplifying diverse Appalachian voices\n\nMusic and dance have b
 een a vital part of the Folk School since its founding in 1925. As we celeb
 rate our 100th year\, Centennial Sounds honors this legacy by spotlighting 
 the cultural richness of Appalachian music and the many voices that shape i
 t. This special performance series will feature five headliners whose work 
 expands and redefines the story of Appalachian music. Through these concert
 s\, we aim to create new opportunities for our community in Western North C
 arolina to experience the full spectrum of Appalachian sound.\n\nThe Folk S
 chool is supported by the North Carolina Arts Council\, a division of the D
 epartment of Natural and Cultural Resources.
DTEND:20260728T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035733Z
DTSTART:20260727T230000Z
GEO:35.03748;-83.964153
LOCATION:Folk School Festival Barn
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Centennial Sounds
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52737244008951
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/centennial-sounds-5477
END:VEVENT
