BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation,Outdoor Recreation (kayak, paddle, hikes),N
 ature & Wildlife Programs
DESCRIPTION:Join us at The Park at Seven Devils for some backyard birding! 
 Birding is an activity that can be done by anyone at any age. Most birders 
 start out by identifying common birds found at their backyard bird feeders.
  During this workshop you will learn how to point out key characteristics\,
  such as size\, coloration\, and activity\, that can help you identify comm
 on backyard bird species\, specifically species that visit bird feeders. By
  using applications like Audubon and Merlin\, along with identification gui
 des\, you will be able to use those key characteristics to help you identif
 y common species found here in the High Country. Binoculars are not require
 d\, but highly recommended\, and there will be a quick lesson on how to pro
 perly use binoculars. This is a Ranger Workshop with The Town of Seven Devi
 ls.
DTEND:20260812T143000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035734Z
DTSTART:20260812T130000Z
GEO:36.14599;-81.797599
LOCATION:The Park at Seven Devils
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Ranger Workshop - Backyard Birding
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51815547957421
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/ranger-workshop-backyard-birding
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:March 14 – August 23\, 2026\n\nIn the ultimate battle for survi
 val\, every animal has a plan.\n\nExplore the striking ways nature fights b
 ack in “Staying Alive\,” featuring 17 live animals from around the world wi
 th unbelievable self-defense strategies. Come face to face with trippy toad
 s\, armored armadillos\, a two-toed sloth and more.\n\nDiscover how these d
 efenders deploy an amazing arsenal of high-fashion camouflage and mimicry\,
  specialized armor and advanced chemical warfare – like stink bombs\, caboo
 se cannons and smoke screens – to hide in plain sight\, stand their ground 
 or even drop a limb and make a run for it. Enjoy live animal encounters\, l
 arger-than-life sculptures\, 3D tactile experiences and interactive program
 s.\n\nPerfect for families and animal enthusiasts of all ages. Offered in E
 nglish & Spanish.
DTEND:20260812T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035734Z
DTSTART:20260812T140000Z
GEO:35.782156;-78.639336
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Staying Alive 
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52207083034931
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/staying-alive
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations,Reenactments & Living History
DESCRIPTION:Learn about one of the small arms (musket\, flintlock\, or rifl
 e) that a soldier stationed at Fort Macon would have carried and used.\n\nT
 his will include a blank firing demonstration of the weapon.\nMeet in the f
 ort parade ground.\n\n \n\nPhoto by Jairus Hill : Living historian demonstr
 ating a musket at Fort Macon State Park.
DTEND:20260812T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035734Z
DTSTART:20260812T143000Z
GEO:34.696366;-76.684506
LOCATION:Fort Macon State Park\, Fort Parade Ground
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Small Arms Demonstration
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51922179186894
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/small-arms-demonstration-6298
END:VEVENT
