BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations,Reenactments & Living History
DESCRIPTION:We're going back to our roots.\n\nThis season\, Hickory Ridge H
 istory Museum proudly reintroduces Living History Museum Days\, a return to
  the immersive\, hands-on spirit that once defined us as Hickory Ridge Livi
 ng History Museum and “village”. On select days this summer\, the cabins wi
 ll come alive with the sights\, sounds\, and smells of 18th-century life in
  the North Carolina mountains.\n\nFrom open-hearth cooking and blacksmithin
 g to weaving\, spinning\, woodworking\, and frontier chores\, guests will e
 xperience a day in the life of the early settlers who called this region ho
 me. Our interpreters and volunteers will demonstrate traditional skills thr
 oughout the village\, inviting you to explore\, ask questions\, and connect
  with the everyday stories of Appalachian history.\n\nWhether you’re a long
 time visitor or discovering us for the first time\, Living History Museum D
 ays are your chance to step deeper into the past and to be part of its futu
 re.\n\nInterested in volunteering or learning an 18th-century skill? We’re 
 always looking for new hands to help bring the holler to life. Reach out to
  learn more about becoming part of SAHA family!
DTEND:20260815T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035734Z
DTSTART:20260815T140000Z
GEO:36.208683;-81.669982
LOCATION:Hickory Ridge History Museum
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Living History Museum Days at Hickory Ridge History Museum in Boone
 \, NC
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52543890011455
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/living-history-museum-days-at-hickory-
 ridge-history-museum-in-boone-nc
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:March 14 – August 23\, 2026\n\nIn the ultimate battle for survi
 val\, every animal has a plan.\n\nExplore the striking ways nature fights b
 ack in “Staying Alive\,” featuring 17 live animals from around the world wi
 th unbelievable self-defense strategies. Come face to face with trippy toad
 s\, armored armadillos\, a two-toed sloth and more.\n\nDiscover how these d
 efenders deploy an amazing arsenal of high-fashion camouflage and mimicry\,
  specialized armor and advanced chemical warfare – like stink bombs\, caboo
 se cannons and smoke screens – to hide in plain sight\, stand their ground 
 or even drop a limb and make a run for it. Enjoy live animal encounters\, l
 arger-than-life sculptures\, 3D tactile experiences and interactive program
 s.\n\nPerfect for families and animal enthusiasts of all ages. Offered in E
 nglish & Spanish.
DTEND:20260815T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035734Z
DTSTART:20260815T140000Z
GEO:35.782156;-78.639336
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Staying Alive 
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52207083038006
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/staying-alive
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
DESCRIPTION:Learn about one of the small arms (musket\, flintlock\, or rifl
 e) that a soldier stationed at Fort Macon would have carried and used.\n\nT
 his will include a blank firing demonstration of the weapon.\nMeet in the f
 ort parade ground.\n\n \n\nPhoto by Jairus Hill : Living historian demonstr
 ating a musket at Fort Macon State Park.
DTEND:20260815T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035734Z
DTSTART:20260815T143000Z
GEO:34.696366;-76.684506
LOCATION:Fort Macon State Park
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Small Arms Demonstration 10:30am & 2:30pm
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52019009728034
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/small-arms-demonstration-1030am-230pm
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Guided Tours
DESCRIPTION:Step into Tryon Palace and explore Diana Gabaldon’s award-winni
 ng Outlander series. Learn about the lives of the fictional Jamie and Clair
 e Fraser\, their family and friends\, and interactions with historical figu
 res and events in the tumultuous period of the American Revolution.\n\nTour
  covers storylines from Outlander books 4 – 8 and the Starz Outlander seaso
 ns 4 – 8. (For those not current on the books or show\, there will be spoil
 ers for these books and seasons.)\n\nTour begins at 301 George Street\, acr
 oss from the Tryon Palace Main Gates. Ticket holders should check in at the
  Waystation ticketing desk no later than 3:30 p.m.
DTEND:20260815T204500Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035734Z
DTSTART:20260815T194500Z
GEO:35.104831;-77.043044
LOCATION:Tryon Palace Historic Sites and Gardens
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Discover Tryon Palace: Outlander
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51931164601101
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/discover-tryon-palace-outlander
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
DESCRIPTION:Pretend you’ve been recruited as a member of the Culper Spy Rin
 g\, and you need to know how to decipher a message written in invisible ink
 . Supplies include a paint brush\, water\, drying cloth\, vitriol (diluted 
 sulfuric acid)\, Thomas Jefferson cipher and “furnace box.” Read the clues 
 to find the coin with a hidden message\, reveal the message using the brush
  and vitriol\, then use the cipher to decode the message.\n\nContact: Nancy
  Locquet Absillis\, nancy.locquet@naturalsciences.org
DTSTAMP:20260508T035734Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260816
GEO:35.782156;-78.639336
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY: Spy Training 101: Decode a Secret Message
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52504709731075
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/spy-training-101-decode-a-secret-messa
 ge
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Homeschool & Education Days,Exhibits & Tours,
 Special Site Programs,Outdoor & Recreation,Outdoor Recreation (kayak, paddl
 e, hikes),Nature & Wildlife Programs,Youth & Family Activities
DESCRIPTION:Join the Curious Minds Adventure Scavenger Hunt at Elk Knob Sta
 te Park. Journey through northern hardwood forest\, follow winding mountain
  trails\, and explore the unique ecosystems of this high-elevation park. Ke
 ep your eyes open—what signs of wildlife or weather-shaped landscapes will 
 you uncover? Look for unique rocks that make Elk Knob a very special clue i
 n North Carolina’s geologic history. Start at the Visitor Center and scan t
 he QR code in your Actionbound app. Flyers with the QR code will be placed 
 in the Park Office and on all park map kiosks. \n\nThe adventures are avail
 able on the Actionbound app – a free download to your cellphone through you
 r phone’s app store. There’s no need to create a profile and no personal da
 ta is collected with Actionbound. You simply find new hunts by searching fo
 r the park name or scanning the associated QR code posted for your park’s a
 dventure.\n\nThis program is made possible through a partnership with the N
 C Science Trail (ncsciencetrail.org)! Visit their website for more Curious 
 Minds Adventure Scavenger Hunts being held in other NC State Parks and for 
 other programs being offered throughout the state. \n\nThis scavenger hunt 
 is running now through August 31\, 2026.
DTEND:20260817T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035734Z
DTSTART:20260816T110000Z
GEO:36.333462;-81.696432
LOCATION:Elk Knob State Park
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Elk Knob State Park: Curious Minds Adventure Scavenger Hunt
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52745325350416
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/elk-knob-state-park-curious-minds-adve
 nture-scavenger-hunt
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Exhibitions,Education Programs,Youth & Family A
 ctivities
DESCRIPTION:The Village of Pinehurst will be displaying two of the NC Depar
 tment of Natural & Cultural Resources exhibits throughout 2026.\n\n"Forging
  a Nation" will be on display at the Cannon Park Community Center\, 210 Rat
 tlesnake Trail\, Pinehurst\, NC 28374.\n\n"People of Colonial North Carolin
 a" will be on display at Assembly Hall\, 395 Magnolia Rd.\, Pinehurst\, NC 
 28374.\n\nThe Given Memorial Library & Tufts Archives (150 Cherokee Road\, 
 Pinehurst\, NC 28374) will also have smaller versions of the exhibits on di
 splay throughout the year and will rotate between the different exhibit sub
 jects periodically.
DTEND:20260816T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035734Z
DTSTART:20260816T123000Z
GEO:35.203585;-79.459138
LOCATION:Village of Pinehurst
