BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Panels & Book Discussions
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for the June meeting of the America 250 NC Virtu
 al Book Club! We will be discussing Katharine\, the Wright Sister by Tracey
  Enerson Wood  on August 26 at 6p.\n\nThis historical fiction novel tells t
 he story of the Wright brothers' path to first in flight and their sister's
  important role in their journey.\n\nPlease read the book prior to the disc
 ussion. We recommend borrowing from your local library. \n\nFree and open t
 o the public. No membership required. Come to whichever book talks spark yo
 ur interest. \n\nMeeting Link\n\nMore Information\n\nSign up for an Email R
 eminder
DTEND:20260826T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035734Z
DTSTART:20260826T220000Z
LOCATION:
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Virtual Book Club: Katharine\, the Wright Sister by Tracey Enerson 
 Wood 
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52808292434846
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/virtual-book-club-katharine-the-wright
 -sister-by-tracey-enerson-wood
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
DESCRIPTION:This program honors Evelyn Pope by reading books. \n\nEvelyn\, 
 a college librarian born in 1908 and died in 1995\, loved a variety of book
 s from The Adventures of Tom Sawyer to Shakespeare and James Baldwin. The p
 rogram brings community members together monthly at the museum to discuss b
 ooks\, focusing on works by Black writers or featuring Black subjects\, inc
 luding fiction and non-fiction. Discussions will use questions to facilitat
 e conversation.\n\n"Mama Day" by Gloria Naylor\nWednesday\, Feb. 25\n "The 
 Black Angels: The Untold Story of the Nurses Who Helped Cure Tuberculosis" 
 by Maria Smilios\nWednesday\, April 22\n "A Visitation of Spirits" by Randa
 ll Kenan\nWednesday\, June 24\n "Becoming Lunsford Lane: The Lives of an Am
