 s
DESCRIPTION:Heritage Weekend\n\nSeptember 19-20\, 2026 | Folk Art Center Gr
 ounds\nA two-day celebration of Appalachian traditions including broom-maki
 ng\, basketry\, instrument making\, storytelling\, and mountain music. Free
  and open to the public. The Kids Activity Table will feature hands-on craf
 ts for children of all ages.
DTEND:20260919T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035735Z
DTSTART:20260919T140000Z
GEO:35.592745;-82.481791
LOCATION:Folk Art Center\, Southern Highland Craft Guild\, Auditorium / Out
 side 
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Heritage Weekend
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51523677783942
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/heritage-weekend
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations,Reenactments & Living History,Exhi
 bits & Tours,Special Site Programs,Education Programs,Youth & Family Activi
 ties
DESCRIPTION:Experience life in the Southern Appalachian backcountry during 
 the American Revolution at our Militia Muster! Guests of all ages are invit
 ed to step into the world of 18th-century militia life through interactive 
 demonstrations\, reenactments\, and hands-on activities.\n\nWatch as 18th C
 entury Militia reenactors bring history to life through drills\, camp life\
 , and mock recruitment scenes. Explore the daily challenges faced by settle
 rs and soldiers\, and learn more about what it took to fight for independen
 ce in the mountains of North Carolina.\n\nThis is a family-friendly\, immer
 sive educational event perfect for history lovers\, homeschool families\, a
 nd curious visitors of all ages.\n\nPlease call 828-264-2120 for ticketing 
 information.
DTEND:20260919T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035735Z
DTSTART:20260919T150000Z
GEO:36.208683;-81.669982
LOCATION:Hickory Ridge History Museum
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Militia Muster Event - Experience 18th Century
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52543913626450
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/militia-muster-event-experience-18th-c
 entury
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Guided Tours
DESCRIPTION:Step into Tryon Palace and explore Diana Gabaldon’s award-winni
 ng Outlander series. Learn about the lives of the fictional Jamie and Clair
 e Fraser\, their family and friends\, and interactions with historical figu
 res and events in the tumultuous period of the American Revolution.\n\nTour
  covers storylines from Outlander books 4 – 8 and the Starz Outlander seaso
 ns 4 – 8. (For those not current on the books or show\, there will be spoil
 ers for these books and seasons.)\n\nTour begins at 301 George Street\, acr
 oss from the Tryon Palace Main Gates. Ticket holders should check in at the
  Waystation ticketing desk no later than 3:30 p.m.
DTEND:20260919T204500Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035735Z
DTSTART:20260919T194500Z
GEO:35.104831;-77.043044
LOCATION:Tryon Palace Historic Sites and Gardens
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Discover Tryon Palace: Outlander
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51931164602126
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/discover-tryon-palace-outlander
END:VEVENT
