 -park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Transylvania Heritage Museum in Brevard for our 
 new exhibit celebrating America's 250th anniversary. Discover how Revolunti
 onary War veterans\, including Transylvania County Patriots\, carried the s
 pirit of liberty from battlefields into the rugged Appalachian frontier. Th
 rough artifacts\, stories and hands-on experiences - including our Revoluti
 on Era Garden - explore the journey from conflict to community in the mount
 ains we call home!\n\nOpen Thursday through Saturday 12 p.m. to 4 p.m. Free
  and open to all. Donations accepted
DTEND:20261017T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035736Z
DTSTART:20261017T160000Z
GEO:35.234922;-82.737524
LOCATION:Transylvania Heritage Museum 
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Battlefields to Backwoods Soldiers Shaping Applachia  Celebrating A
 merica's 250th
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52780900772707
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/battlefields-to-backwoods-soldiers-sha
 ping-applachia-celebrating-americas-250th
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations,Reenactments & Living History
DESCRIPTION:Trail to Victory: The Story of Kings Mountain invites you on an
  unforgettable journey through time. Step into the heart of the 1780 Kings 
 Mountain Campaign and witness the pivotal events that shaped the American R
 evolution.\n\nThis immersive museum experience leads you into the heart of 
 the harrowing events leading up to the October 7\, 1780 battle\, places you
  amidst the chaos of the conflict\, and allows you to experience the battle
 's repercussions from the perspectives of both Patriots and British soldier
 s.\n\nJoin us for three museum tours on Saturday\, October 17th\, starting 
 at 12:00 PM\, 1:30 PM\, and 2:30 PM. Tickets are available day of at the Ho
 rn in the West Ticket Office.
DTEND:20261017T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035736Z
DTSTART:20261017T160000Z
GEO:36.208683;-81.669982
LOCATION:Hickory Ridge History Museum
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Trail to Victory: The Story of Kings Mountain
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52506317161126
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/trail-to-victory-the-story-of-kings-mo
 untain
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Performances & Arts,Theater & Musicals
DESCRIPTION:​Spill the Tea! is a bold new musical inspired by the first rec
 orded act of women's activism in American history — the Edenton Tea Party. 
 At the heart of the story is Penelope Barker\, the daring woman who organiz
 ed 50 other women to sign a public resolution boycotting British goods — an
 d sent it directly to King George III. This radical act of defiance\, carri
 ed out in a time when women had no political voice\, helped spark a revolut
 ion and laid the groundwork\, not only for the birth of a new nation\, but 
 for women to stand up for their rights.\n\nBlending pop\, hip-hop\, orchest
 ral\, and classic Broadway musical styles\, Spill the Tea! is filled with h
 umor\, heart\, and history. With a witty script plus lavish sets and costum
 es\, the show celebrates the power of those who refused to stay silent.​
DTEND:20261017T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035736Z
DTSTART:20261017T190000Z
GEO:36.299891;-76.219792
LOCATION:Arts of the Albemarle\, Maguire Theatre
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Spill the Tea!
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52507714085620
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/spill-the-tea-7522
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Guided Tours
DESCRIPTION:Step into Tryon Palace and explore Diana Gabaldon’s award-winni
 ng Outlander series. Learn about the lives of the fictional Jamie and Clair
 e Fraser\, their family and friends\, and interactions with historical figu
 res and events in the tumultuous period of the American Revolution.\n\nTour
  covers storylines from Outlander books 4 – 8 and the Starz Outlander seaso
 ns 4 – 8. (For those not current on the books or show\, there will be spoil
 ers for these books and seasons.)\n\nTour begins at 301 George Street\, acr
 oss from the Tryon Palace Main Gates. Ticket holders should check in at the
  Waystation ticketing desk no later than 3:30 p.m.
DTEND:20261017T204500Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035736Z
DTSTART:20261017T194500Z
GEO:35.104831;-77.043044
LOCATION:Tryon Palace Historic Sites and Gardens
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Discover Tryon Palace: Outlander
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51931164602127
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/discover-tryon-palace-outlander
END:VEVENT
