BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
DESCRIPTION:The Clarion Call of Liberty and Independence\, April 26\, 2026\
 n\nContinuing Wilmington Water Tours’ commemoration of the United State’s 2
 50th anniversary\, join Dr. Chris E. Fonvielle Jr.\, Professor Emeritus in 
 the Dept. of History at UNCW continues discussing the decline of the Britis
 h Empire after the French and Indian War in 1763 and the rise of a great na
 tion by 1887.  This cruise covers an in-depth discussion about Great Britai
 n’s grand plan for a military campaign against the Southern colonies by way
  of the Cape Fear River in 1776\; and the decisive Battle of Moore’s Creek 
 Bridge based on Dr. Fonvielle’s latest research and forthcoming book.\n\nWh
 ether you’re a lifelong history buff or just curious about the forces that 
 shaped this region\, this is a one-of-a-kind opportunity to learn while enj
 oying a relaxing\, scenic cruise. Topics rotate monthly\, so every trip off
 ers a new perspective on Wilmington’s place in American history.  The next 
 two cruises will be April 26\, and May 24.\n\nOur boat\, The Wilmington\, h
 as comfortable seating for up to 49 passengers\, refreshments for all ages 
 at the bar and a restroom on board. This is a 90 minute cruise $45 adults\,
  $25 children. Boarding is 15 minutes prior to departure.
DTEND:20261025T153000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035736Z
DTSTART:20261025T140000Z
GEO:34.232504;-77.949383
LOCATION:Wilmington Water Tours LLC\, On the Riverwalk
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:History Comes Alive with Historian Dr. Chris Fonvielle
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52683590244829
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/history-comes-alive-with-historian-dr-
 chris-fonvielle-4988
END:VEVENT
