BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations,Reenactments & Living History
DESCRIPTION:Prepare to celebrate and enjoy festive Scottish traditions for 
 New Year’s Eve (Hogmanay) and the Yule season. Enjoy speaking to Revolution
 ary soldiers of the NC Highland and 71st Regiments\, listen to Gaelic music
  and storytelling\, learn about tartan history and see traditional Hogmanay
  dishes made over an open fire\, and more. We encourage you to dress in you
 r family tartan or plaid! Food not available to the public. FREE. All ages 
 welcome. Drop-in.
DTEND:20261219T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035736Z
DTSTART:20261219T150000Z
GEO:35.979741;-79.992174
LOCATION:High Point Museum
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Scottish Faire in Historical Park 
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51825997978629
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/scottish-faire-in-historical-park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations,Ceremonies & Anniversaries
DESCRIPTION:The local observance of National Wreaths Across America Day is 
 planned for Saturday\, December 19\, at 12:00 noon at the Taylorsville Ceme
 tery. Daughters of the American Revolution (DAR) – Carolina Emerald Chapter
  will host a Sons of the American Revolution musket volley as part of the e
 vent.
DTEND:20261219T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035736Z
DTSTART:20261219T170000Z
GEO:35.919768;-81.167624
LOCATION:Taylorsville Cemetery
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:National Wreaths Across America Day
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51826571452081
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/national-wreaths-across-america-day
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations,Reenactments & Living History,Exhi
 bits & Tours,Open Houses,Special Site Programs
DESCRIPTION:We cordially invite you to see Aycock Birthplace in a new light
 . Tour our historic buildings with costumed interpreters by candlelight and
  watch the preparation of a Christmas meal on a hearth all while learning a
 bout historical Christmas and New Years traditions. Admission is $5.00 (plu
 s tax)\, admission is free for visitors aged 12 and under.\nMore informatio
 n and details to be announced as the event approaches.
DTEND:20261220T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260508T035736Z
DTSTART:20261219T220000Z
GEO:35.520185;-77.976051
LOCATION:Governor Charles B. Aycock Birthplace
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Christmas Candlelight Open House
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52207273191307
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/christmas-candlelight-open-house-2836
END:VEVENT
