BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
DESCRIPTION:This exhibit tells the stories of seven everyday North Carolini
 ans and extraordinary leaders — Gertrude Weil\, Henry Owl\, Joe Lewis\, Abr
 aham Galloway\, Ronald Mace\, James Hunter\, and Willa Player — who petitio
 ned\, protested\, and organized to expand democracy. The exhibit explores c
 hange\, freedom\, civic responsibility\, and overcoming challenges by telli
 ng the story of a few North Carolinians who have raised their voices to cal
 l out injustice and fully participate in our democratic society.
DTSTAMP:20260508T035736Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270104
GEO:36.092774;-79.436435
LOCATION:May Memorial Library
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Making Our Voices Heard (America 250 NC Traveling Exhibit) 
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52569559729991
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/making-our-voices-heard
END:VEVENT
